### Rules for Frontend

- You must pay attention to visual clarity and contrast. Do not place white text on a white background.
- You must ensure the UX is pleasant. Boxes should grow to fit their contents, etc. 
- When asking the user for sensitive information - you must use password style text-entry boxes in the UI.
- You should use Next.js as it works best with Vercel. 
- This frontend will ultimately be deployed on Vercel, but it should be possible to test locally. 
- Always provide users with a way to run the created UI once you have created it.
## Visual Theme: Scientific Atelier

### Overall Design Philosophy
Create a sophisticated, welcoming, and modern AI application
that feels like a research studio rather than a conventional
corporate dashboard.

The interface should communicate curiosity, intelligence,
trustworthiness, creativity, and human-centered innovation.

### Color Palette
- Primary background: Midnight Navy (#101B32)
- Secondary surfaces: Deep Cobalt (#254D79)
- Primary accent: Teal (#37C9BA)
- Light background: Warm Ivory (#F4F6F4)
- Decorative accent: Muted Gold (#D8AD75)
- Main text on dark backgrounds: Ivory (#F4F6F4)
- Main text on light backgrounds: Midnight Navy (#101B32)

### Typography
- Use elegant, contemporary sans-serif typography.
- Prioritize readability, hierarchy, and generous spacing.
- Use larger typography for primary messages.
- Avoid overly dense or cluttered layouts.

### Interface Components
- Use softly rounded cards and buttons.
- Incorporate subtle shadows and refined borders.
- Use teal for primary interactive elements.
- Use gold sparingly for decorative emphasis.
- Include thoughtful hover states and transitions.
- Maintain consistent spacing throughout the application.

### User Experience
- Make the interface intuitive for nontechnical users.
- Use clear instructions and descriptive labels.
- Provide helpful loading states and error messages.
- Ensure mobile and desktop responsiveness.
- Maintain accessible color contrast and keyboard navigation.

### AI Interaction Design
- Design the AI interaction as a thoughtful conversation.
- Clearly distinguish user inputs from AI responses.
- Make system status and processing activity visible.
- Provide graceful handling of incomplete or failed requests.
- Never expose API keys or other sensitive credentials.
## Official Technical Documentation

When building or modifying this application, consult
the following official documentation:

- Next.js: https://nextjs.org/docs
- Vercel: https://vercel.com/docs

Use these sources to verify current implementation patterns,
APIs, routing, configuration, and deployment practices.

Follow the most current stable documentation relevant
to the project's installed framework versions.

Prioritize official documentation over outdated examples.
### Design Constraints
- Avoid generic AI imagery such as glowing robot heads.
- Prefer abstract scientific patterns and subtle geometric forms.
- Favor clarity and meaningful interaction over decoration.
- Keep the application polished without sacrificing performance.
- Use Next.js and maintain compatibility with Vercel deployment.